From cac130d748f8c5c845a6613acd5441016a30d033 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan Ahern <danahern@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Feb 2026 12:46:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix OSPI flash programmer: DFS=16 for all DDR Octal ops,
 fixed timing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: status register read with DFS=8 returns 0 in DDR Octal mode,
so WIP polling never waited — erase/program operations raced. Also changed
page program command from 0x84 to 0x12 (both valid in OPI DDR mode).

Key fixes:
- Use DFS=16 (ospi_setup_write_ddr16) for Write Enable, erase, program
- Replace broken status register polling with fixed delays (500ms erase,
  2ms page program) since ospi_setup_read with DFS=8 is unreliable in DDR
- Send Software Reset (0x66/0x99) after programming, then full re-init
  via setup_flash_xip() for reliable XIP restore
- Convert XIP addresses to flash-relative for erase/program commands
- Add D-cache flush/invalidate for MRAM flag and XIP verify reads

Verified: 2.2MB kernel programmed to OSPI, XIP readback matches source,
normal boot from OSPI XIP works on subsequent power cycles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
